# =============================================================================
# Build context exclusions
# =============================================================================
# Without this file `COPY . .` pulls the entire working directory into the build
# context — including the secrets and the 300 MB of build output. It is also
# uploaded to the Docker daemon on every build, so a large context makes each
# build noticeably slower even when the Dockerfile copies nothing.
# =============================================================================

# --- Secrets: never in an image layer ---------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
client/.env.local
client/.env.local.example
# Belt and braces. Coolify injects these at runtime, so no image can contain one.
*.pem
*.key

# --- Version control ---------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore

# --- Build output (regenerated inside the image) -----------------------------
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
dist
**/dist
build
**/build
out
**/out

# --- Caches ------------------------------------------------------------------
.cache
**/.cache
.turbo
**/.turbo
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.vscode
.idea

# --- Logs and local artefacts ------------------------------------------------
*.log
npm-debug.log*
coverage
**/coverage

# --- Docs and tests ----------------------------------------------------------
# Not needed to build or run either service. Excluding docs keeps the context
# small; tests are excluded for the same reason, and the gates still run in CI
# against the repository rather than the image.
docs
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.spec.ts

# --- OS cruft ----------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db